# Playwright
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/

# Lock files ARE committed here, overriding ~/.gitignore_global.
# Reproducible builds are a gate requirement: the exact mitmproxy pin
# (REQ PXY-006) is meaningless without a resolved lock, and the security
# gate's audit results only mean something against a fixed dependency set.
!*.lock
!uv.lock
!package-lock.json

# Shipped package data, never ignored.
#
# `daemon/src/pporlock/data/exclusions-default.yaml` — the 33 default
# ClientHello exclusions (REQ PXY-013) — was absent from this repository from
# the first commit until 0.9.0, because a *global* gitignore on the author's
# machine ignored any directory named `data`. `git status` was clean, the tests
# passed, and every clone shipped a proxy that would decrypt OS update
# endpoints, certificate revocation, and banking hosts.
#
# A repository .gitignore takes precedence over the global one, so this
# negation is what stops a personal ignore rule deciding what this project
# ships. Found by CI on its first run.
!daemon/src/pporlock/data/
!daemon/src/pporlock/data/**
